Q: How to differentiate context for a clipboard button in a dynamic DataTemplate? A: <p>Using <a href="https://www.nuget.org/packages/CommunityToolkit.Mvvm" rel="nofollow noreferrer">CommunityToolkit.Mvvm</a> we can refactor @galex's answer to make the object observable with property changed notification and reduce the amount of boiler-plate code you need to write for ICommands.</p>
<pre class="lang-cs prettyprint-override"><code>public partial class GridInfoItem : ObservableObject
{
    [ObservableProperty] public string? Name { get; set; }
    [ObservableProperty] public string? Value { get; set; }
    [ObservableProperty] public string? Clipboard_Button { get; set; }
    [RelayCommand]
    public async Task ButtonClicked()
    {
        await Clipboard.Default.SetTextAsync(Value);
    }
}
</code></pre>
